# Style & conventions (DAT)

TypeScript
- Keep types strict; avoid `any` unless there is a clear reason.
- Prefer explicit types on public functions/exports and API boundaries.
- Prefer `unknown` + narrowing over `any` when unsure.

Next.js / App Router
- Follow existing project patterns before creating new abstractions.
- Avoid introducing new server/client boundaries unless required.
- Prefer minimal server-safe changes; avoid "magic" global side effects.

Prisma / DB
- Preserve organization scoping and tenancy boundaries.
- Do not introduce schema/migration changes unless explicitly requested.
- Prefer query changes that are easy to review (no cleverness).

General
- Small functions, small diffs.
- No unrelated refactors, renames, formatting sweeps, or “cleanup” unless asked.
- Keep behavior changes measurable: explain what changes in runtime behavior.